# /new-partial

## What This Does

Creates a new ERB partial in `app/views/<resource>/_<name>.html.erb`. Documents
the partial's contract with a **strict locals** magic comment (Rails 7.1+) so
Rails raises on a missing or unknown local.

## Usage

```
/new-partial profiles form
/new-partial shared header
/new-partial layouts flash_messages
```

## How It Works

### 1. Read Patterns

- `.claude/styles/{{ 'styles/erb-style.md' | installed(stack) }}`
- Existing partials in `app/views/` for project conventions

### 2. Determine Locals Contract

What does the caller need to provide? Declare it on the first line of the
partial: `<%# locals: (profile:, submit_label: nil) -%>`. Required locals have
no default; optional ones get one. `<%# locals: () -%>` means "takes no locals".

### 3. Generate the Partial

#### Form partial: `app/views/profiles/_form.html.erb`

```erb
<%# locals: (profile:, submit_label: nil) -%>
<%# profile: Profile (new or persisted); submit_label: optional String %>
<% submit_label ||= profile.persisted? ? t('common.update') : t('common.create') %>

<%= form_with(model: profile, class: "{{ v.css.form }}") do |form| %>
  <% if profile.errors.any? %>
    <div role="alert" class="{{ v.css.errors }}">
      <h2 class="{{ c.errors_title }}">
        <%= t('errors.messages.validation_failed', count: profile.errors.count) %>
      </h2>
      <ul class="{{ v.css.errors_list }}">
        <% profile.errors.full_messages.each do |msg| %>
          <li><%= msg %></li>
        <% end %>
      </ul>
    </div>
  <% end %>

  <div>
    <%= form.label :name, class: "{{ v.css.label }}" %>
    <%= form.text_field :name,
                        required: true,
                        class: "{{ v.css.input }}" %>
  </div>

  <div>
    <%= form.label :email, class: "{{ v.css.label }}" %>
    <%= form.email_field :email,
                          class: "{{ v.css.input }}" %>
  </div>

  <div class="{{ c.form_actions }}">
    <%= link_to t('common.cancel'), :back, class: "{{ c.btn_secondary }}" %>
    <%= form.submit submit_label, class: "{{ v.css.button }}" %>
  </div>
<% end %>
```

Caller (with explicit `locals:`):

```erb
<%= render "form", profile: @profile %>
<%= render "form", profile: @profile, submit_label: t('profiles.update') %>
```

#### Shared partial: `app/views/shared/_header.html.erb`

```erb
<%# locals: (user:) -%>

<header class="{{ c.nav_bar }}">
  <div class="{{ c.nav_inner }}">
    <%= link_to root_path, class: "{{ c.brand }}" do %>
      <%= t('app.name') %>
    <% end %>

    <nav class="{{ c.nav }}">
      <%= link_to t('navigation.profiles'), profiles_path %>
      <%# session_path: Rails 8 auth generator; Devise uses destroy_user_session_path %>
      <%= button_to t('navigation.sign_out'), session_path,
                    method: :delete,
                    {{ confirm_signout }} %>
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
```

### 4. Verify

The template syntax is checked at render time. To verify quickly:

```bash
bin/rails runner 'puts ApplicationController.render(template: "profiles/index", assigns: { profiles: [] })'
# Or run a system spec that exercises the view
```

## Rules

- Declare strict locals on the first line: `<%# locals: (profile:, size: :md) -%>`
- Always pass locals **explicitly**: `render "form", profile: @profile`
- NEVER rely on instance variables (`@profile`) in a partial — break encapsulation
{% if v.vc %}- If a partial needs >3 locals, consider promoting it to a ViewComponent
{% elif v.phlex %}- If a partial needs >3 locals, consider promoting it to a Phlex component
{% else %}- If a partial needs >3 locals, split it or move logic into a helper/presenter
{% endif %}
- Use `t('...')` for all strings
- Provide ARIA roles on dynamic alerts/status regions
- Give optional locals their default in the strict-locals signature

{% if v.vc or v.phlex %}
## Partial vs {{ 'ViewComponent' if v.vc else 'Phlex component' }} — When to choose

Choose a partial when:
- The markup is mostly static
- Used only in 1–2 places
- No conditional class logic

Choose a {{ 'ViewComponent' if v.vc else 'Phlex component' }} when:
- 3+ usages
- Variants (size, color, state)
- Computed class names
- Slots needed (header / body / footer)
- You want a unit-testable rendering

{% endif %}
## Output

```
Created:
  app/views/profiles/_form.html.erb

Locals contract:
  <%# locals: (profile:, submit_label: nil) -%>

Caller example:
  <%= render "form", profile: @profile %>
```
